    {
      "chunk_id": "ragchunk_72f967052c2f9dc3",
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/05_operations/remote_runner_design_runbook.md",
        "line_start": 141,
        "line_end": 149,
        "title": "doc_id: \"POST-H-021-REMOTE-RUNNER-DESIGN-RUNBOOK\""
      },
      "fragment": "```text\nremote runner design != remote execution enabled\nremote readiness != remote-ready claim\nsecure transport design != secure transport implemented\nprotocol matrix != network allowed\nADR-3 != runtime enablement\n```\n\nNo se habilitan red, transporte activo, shell remoto, credenciales, external APIs ni workers remotos. Cualquier cambio de esta frontera requiere ADR/backlog posterior, sandbox remoto, Approval/RBAC, command allowlist, observabilidad, kill-switch, rollback y pruebas adversariales.",
